# Adaptive and Responsive Design Implementation Plan

The objective is to ensure the GHG Reporting application is fully functional and visually appealing on tablets and mobile devices.

## Proposed Changes

### [CSS Layer]

#### [MODIFY] [dashboard-dark.css](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/dashboard-dark.css)
- Add media queries for Tablet (`max-width: 1024px`) and Mobile (`max-width: 768px`).
- **Sidebar**:
    - Hide sidebar by default on tablet/mobile and add a `.sidebar-open` class to show it as an overlay (drawer).
    - Add transition effects for the drawer.
- **Main Content**:
    - Remove `overflow: hidden` from body if needed or ensure inner containers handle scroll.
    - Adjust `dashboard-grid` to a single column on tablet/mobile.
- **Top Bar**:
    - Add a hamburger menu button (menu icon) that appears only on mobile.
- **Containers**:
    - Reduce padding in `.dashboard-grid`, `.calculator-container`, and `.top-bar`.

### [Javascript Layer]

#### [NEW] [mobile-menu.js](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/mobile-menu.js)
- Implement a simple script to toggle the `.sidebar-open` class on the sidebar when the hamburger menu is clicked.
- Add an overlay to close the sidebar when clicking outside.

### [HTML Layer]

#### [MODIFY] [dashboard.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/dashboard.html), [emission-selection.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/emission-selection.html), [emission-factor.html](file:///c:/Users/samsung/Desktop/ghg%20old/public/emission-factor.html)
- Include the hamburger menu SVG in the `.breadcrumbs` or `.top-bar` area.
- Link the new `mobile-menu.js`.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Use the browser tool to verify the presence of the toggle button and test clicking it on mobile resolutions.

### Manual Verification
- Resize the browser window to verify all breakpoints.
- Check that the dashboard grid stacks correctly.
- Ensure the sidebar drawer opens and closes as expected on mobile.
- Verify horizontal scrolling for tables.
